{
  "case_id": "2001-01-518",
  "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument next in No. 01-518, the BE&K Construction Company v. the National Labor Relations Board."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Maurice Baskin",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner BE&K Construction is asking the Court to hold that the First Amendment protects objectively based lawsuits from being declared unlawful by the National Labor Relations Board."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: How do you describe the test applied by the board?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Maurice Baskin",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a constitutional and statutory argument, which is what the Court itself said in both of these cases because there's a sanction involved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I don't understand that. Why do you say it's been in doubt for most of the 20-year period?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baskin",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BASKIN: Well, it is -- stare decisis is a form of deference, and we're talking about stare decisis would apply to the Court's own opinion. Only this Court is required to defer to itself about its own opinion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: In every 8(a)(1) case, the\nretaliatory motive is found by the board. That's part of\nthe statutory proceeding, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wallace",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think this Court's make it\nquite -- this Court's decisions make it quite clear that\nunder the National Labor Relations Act, it is board rather\nthan courts that have the responsibility of ruling about\nunfair labor practices."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is the courts' -- is the board's\ndefinition of a unmeritorious lawsuit simply one which --\nin which the plaintiff does not get what the plaintiff\nwants. It's thrown out of court, so to speak."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wallace",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALLACE: Well, there is not a reference to\nfee-shifting as such in the National Labor Relations Act,\nbut Congress did say in section 8(a)(1) that it shall be\nan unfair labor practice to an employee to interfere with,\nrestrain, or coerce employees in the exercise of the\nconcerted activity rights for mutual aid and protection\nthat are guaranteed in section 7."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae29edaf5b4967a1b0185288e5b8a62d31d413b47cc9fecdadcef9c97522edc3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae29edaf5b49-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: In other words, Noerr-Pennington\ndoesn't have a constitutional underpinning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2001-01-518",
      "confidence": 0.0,
